      "extract": "Introduction Since its introduction by Charles Stein ([Ste72, Ste86]), the so-called Stein’s method is a corpus of techniques that revealed itself very successful in studying probability approximation and convergence in law (see for instance [CGS11, Cha14, LRS17] and references therein). Much less is known regard- ing the interplay between Stein’s method and functional inequalities. Recently, a series of papers",
